A||||4||zeusrekning||Where is ECM?
Z||000000||zeusrekning||07-21-99||08:59 PM||||I need to check fo my check engine light where is the ecm rekning to check for codes?
Z||000001||87FieroGT||07-21-99||09:21 PM||||The ALDL connector is located behind the small panel that holds the cigarette lighter. It is very easy to gain access to.
Z||000002||SCCA FIERO||07-21-99||09:26 PM||||It is under the console. Remove the shift fascia with the ashtrays. Then remove the console with the little glovebox thing in it. The thing that you need is bolted to the black plastic support you should now see.<p>If you have never taken these things off:<br>remove the ashtrays, then the 4 bolts that hold the shift fascia down. If you have a manual tranny unscrew the shift knob then lift the shift fascia off. If you have an auto, there should be a tab on the knob that needs to be pulled out(i think) then you can lift the fascia assembly out. Then there are 2 bolts at the front of the console that should be exposed now, remove these. There are also 2 screws inside the glovebox thingy, those come out too. The cigarette lighter has to be unpluged or unbolted. You should see the thing you are after :)
Z||000003||SCCA FIERO||07-21-99||09:32 PM||||Well, ignore my post. I just removed the cigarette lighter trim and there it is. You learn something new everyday :) 
Z||000004||theogre||07-22-99||07:41 AM||||the 2 terminals you want are the lower pair on the passemgers side. the connector is upside down.
